Task 3 (Easy): Maximum Profit Analyzer
Problem Description
Given daily profit/loss values, find the maximum possible profit obtainable from a contiguous sequence of days using Kadane’s Algorithm.
Input Format
•	First line contains integer N.
•	Second line contains N integers.
Output Format
Print maximum subarray sum.
Constraints
•	1 ≤ N ≤ 10^5
Sample Input
8
-2 -3 4 -1 -2 1 5 -3
Sample Output
7



Solution:
import java.util.*;
public class Task3 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        int n = sc.nextInt();
        int max = sc.nextInt();
        int sum = max;

        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
            int x = sc.nextInt();
            sum = Math.max(x, sum + x);
            max = Math.max(max, sum);
        }

        System.out.println(max);
    }
}
